WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.520
The Analyze phase asks why the course should exist.

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:06.940
Start with the business, operational, compliance, or performance problem.

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:09.980
Is there a behavior that needs to change?

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:12.260
A task that is performed inconsistently?

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:14.540
A policy that learners must apply?

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:16.440
A decision that causes mistakes?

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:17.960
The clearer the problem,

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:22.140
the easier it becomes to decide what the course should teach.

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:23.660
Audience analysis is central.

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:28.600
Identify who the learners are, what they already know, what they struggle with,

00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:32.020
what language or examples will make sense to them,

00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:34.300
and what constraints affect their participation.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:39.620
A course for new hires needs different pacing than a course for experienced practitioners.

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:45.700
A course for field workers may need different delivery assumptions than a course for office-based staff.

00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:47.980
Task analysis separates information from performance.

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:53.300
People may need information, but training is usually justified because people need to do,

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:55.580
decide, recognize, avoid, or explain something.

00:00:55.580 --> 00:01:00.140
Breaking down the task helps identify required knowledge, common mistakes, decision points,

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:03.560
tools used, and the conditions under which performance happens.

00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:07.360
This prevents the course from becoming a catalog of facts.

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:11.160
Analysis also includes constraints: delivery environment, device expectations, seat time,

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:14.200
accessibility needs, translation needs, regulatory requirements, LMS tracking,

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:16.480
review timelines, and available source material.

00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:18.760
These constraints are not administrative trivia.

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:22.560
They shape course length, media choices, navigation, assessment, and rollout.

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:26.360
Finally, analysis should ask whether eLearning is the right solution.

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:31.680
If the problem is lack of access, broken process design, unclear policy, missing tools,

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:35.480
or poor incentives, a course alone may not fix it.

00:01:35.480 --> 00:01:40.040
ADDIE is strongest when it helps the team define the right intervention,

00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:44.220
even when that intervention includes job aids, manager support, process changes,

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:46.500
or coaching in addition to eLearning.
